  "blocks": [
   {
    "id": "p1",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "In "
     },
     {
      "t": "gloss",
      "v": "Northern Ireland",
      "zh": "北爱尔兰"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": ", a group of "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "archaeologists",
      "ref": "v-archaeologist"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " were looking for a 400-year-old castle. But instead, they found something much older and more surprising—an 8,000-year-old village!"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p2",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "The team was digging near a riverbank when they made the discovery. They found the "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "remains",
      "ref": "v-remains"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " of an ancient house that had been buried for thousands of years. They also uncovered tiny tools left by people from that long-ago time. Some of the tools were made of "
     },
     {
      "t": "gloss",
      "v": "flint",
      "zh": "燧石"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": ". These sharp stones were once used for hunting animals and fishing in the river."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p3",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Pupils from a local primary school joined the dig to help. They worked with other volunteers to support the scientists. The young helpers were very excited about their findings. Ten-year-old Niamh found a small piece of flint in the soil. “I didn’t know what it was at first,” she said. “Then a man told me it was thousands of years old!” Another student added, “It’s fun but "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "messy",
      "ref": "v-messy"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": ". You have to dig carefully with your hands in the mud.”"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p4",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "An archaeologist said the location was perfect for early people to settle. “It’s "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "flat",
      "ref": "v-flat"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": ", near the river for water, with lots of fish and birds for food,” she explained. “It’s "
     },
     {
      "t": "gloss",
      "v": "mind-blowing",
      "zh": "令人惊叹的"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " to find something this old right here where people live today!” The discovery helps us understand how ancient people lived in this area."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "i1",
    "type": "imageRef",
    "image": "img1"
   }
  ]
 },
